  "adaptations": {
    "reason": "Package-private module identities are namespaced for SDK consumers; declarations and writer behavior are preserved. Nearby delegates approval exchange and progress transitions to internal helpers; derived configuration values and identical payload validation are consolidated. Source publication, wire data, actor task ownership and recovery contracts are preserved. Stopping also drains offline import/archive reservations, and their admission waits for the stop registration to retire. Read-only receive inventories expose retained finalized staging and actual unpublished destination occupancy; explicit retries revalidate bounded metadata and payload digests with the same transfer identity. Wire and persisted record formats are unchanged. Outgoing and incoming protocol sessions now execute within the facade-owned reservations and inherited actor isolation; lifecycle, handshake identity, observation state, dispatch uncertainty and receipt/cleanup ordering retain their existing owners and contracts. A package-only ordered observation stream republishes existing events with a receive-release revision, including at subscription and after release, so buffered hint loss cannot hide storage invalidation; application inventory reads reject older results, and public event cases and receipt delivery order remain unchanged.",
